Q: jQuery&#39;s append is not working with an SVG element A: <p>The accepted <a href="https://stackoverflow.com/questions/3642035/jquerys-append-is-not-working-with-an-svg-element/3642265#3642265">answer by <em>bobince</em></a> is a short, portable solution. If you need to not only append SVG but also manipulate it, you could try the <a href="http://pablojs.com" rel="nofollow noreferrer">JavaScript library &quot;Pablo&quot;</a> (I wrote it). It will feel familiar to jQuery users.</p>
<p>Your code example would then look like:</p>
<pre><code>$(document).ready(function() {
    Pablo(&quot;svg&quot;).append('&lt;circle cx=&quot;100&quot; cy=&quot;50&quot; r=&quot;40&quot; stroke=&quot;black&quot; stroke-width=&quot;2&quot; fill=&quot;red&quot;/&gt;');
});
</code></pre>
<p>You can also create SVG elements on the fly, without specifying markup:</p>
<pre><code>var circle = Pablo.circle({
    cx:100,
    cy:50,
    r:40
}).appendTo('svg');
</code></pre>

Q: How do get the differences of a multi dimensional array that have different string keys? A: <p>For simplicity, loop over the stored array and check for related keys in the deletion array. If there are related data sets, compare them with <code>array_diff()</code> and save the result back to the original array. [Demo][1]</p>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>foreach ($imageList as $k =&gt; &amp;$set) {
    $set = array_diff($set, $inputDelete[&quot;{$k}Del&quot;] ?? []);
}
var_export($imageList);
</code></pre>
<p>Output:</p>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>array (
  'lFront' =&gt; 
  array (
    0 =&gt; '20180623_133503.webp',
    1 =&gt; '20180623_135209.webp',
  ),
  'lRear' =&gt; 
  array (
  ),
)
</code></pre>
<p>Looping over the deletion array may have fewer iterations, but it is a little messier to cut off the <code>Del</code> suffix versus appending it as I've done in my above snippet.
[1]: <a href="https://3v4l.org/tm9sU#v" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://3v4l.org/tm9sU#v</a></p>
